---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Val from '../components/Val.astro';
import CancellationPolicy from '../components/CancellationPolicy.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
const s = site.sessions;
---
<Base
  title="FAQ: online counselling questions answered"
  description="Answers to common questions about online counselling with Thehraav: the first session, confidentiality, how online sessions work, languages, payment, cancellations and emergencies."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="FAQ"
    title="Questions you might have."
    lead="It's natural to have questions before starting counselling. If yours isn't answered here, please get in touch."
  />

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container narrow faq">
      <details>
        <summary>What happens in the first session?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            The first session is a gentle conversation. You can share what's been going on, what you'd like to change,
            and ask me anything about how we'd work together. There's no pressure to share more than you're ready to.
            By the end, we'll both have a sense of whether we're a good fit, and what the next steps could be.
          </p>
          <p>
            For new clients, it's free and lasts <Val v={s.freeFirstLength} />. After booking, you'll get an email
            with links to a short consent form and intake form to fill in before we meet.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is it confidential?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Yes. What you share in sessions stays between us. Like all counsellors, I follow professional ethical
            guidelines, and there are a few legal and safety limits, for example if someone's life is at serious risk.
            These are explained clearly in the consent form you receive after booking.
          </p>
          <p>
            To learn how booking details and messages are handled, see the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do online sessions work?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            When you book, you'll get a private video call link by email. At the session time, just click the link.
            There's nothing to install beyond what the link asks for.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Find a quiet, private space</strong> where you won't be overheard or interrupted.</li>
            <li><strong>Use headphones</strong> if you can, for extra privacy.</li>
            <li><strong>Check your internet</strong> and charge your phone or laptop beforehand.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>If you get disconnected, don't worry. Just rejoin using the same link.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Which languages do you offer?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            English and Hindi. Many people switch between the two, and that's completely fine. Speak in whatever
            feels most natural to you.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How does payment work?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            The first session is free for new clients. For regular sessions (<Val v={s.fee} /> for <Val v={s.length} />),
            you pay securely through Razorpay when you book, using UPI, card or netbanking. Your booking is confirmed
            once payment goes through.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What if I need to cancel or reschedule?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <CancellationPolicy />
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is this right for me?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            If you're a woman who often feels overwhelmed by anxiety or by anger that's hard to control, and you'd
            like practical ways to feel calmer and more in control, this could be a good fit. You don't need to have
            everything figured out, or have tried counselling before.
          </p>
          <p>
            Online counselling isn't the right fit for everything. If you're in crisis or need urgent care, please
            reach out to emergency services first. If you're unsure, book a free first session or
            <a href="/contact">send a message</a>, and we can talk it through.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What should I do in an emergency?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            This website, email and WhatsApp are not for emergencies, and messages may not be seen straight away.
          </p>
          <p class="note">
            If you're in crisis or thinking about harming yourself, please call <strong>Tele-MANAS on
            <a href="tel:14416">14416</a></strong> (free, 24/7), or contact your nearest emergency service or hospital
            right away. You can also call <a href="tel:112">112</a>, India's emergency number.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="container narrow center still">
      <p class="lead">Still have a question?</p>
      <div class="btn-row cta-row">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--ghost">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="/book" class="btn">Book a session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .faq details {
    background: var(--white);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .faq summary {
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 1.2rem 3.4rem 1.2rem 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 100;
    font-size: clamp(1.12rem, 2.4vw, 1.3rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--sage-deep);
    line-height: 1.35;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq summary::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    right: 1.4rem;
    top: 50%;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-right: 2px solid var(--terracotta);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--terracotta);
    transform: translateY(-70%) rotate(45deg);
    transition: transform 0.25s;
  }
  .faq details[open] summary::after { transform: translateY(-30%) rotate(-135deg); }
  .answer { padding: 0 1.5rem 1.3rem; }
  .answer > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .answer ul { margin: 0 0 1em; }
  .answer li + li { margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .still { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .still .lead { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .cta-row { justify-content: center; }
</style>
